  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=9$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=9.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=24,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=2A{e}^{2x}+4B{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=24$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2A+4B & =24 \\\\ A+2B & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the two equations from above together, we have the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=9 \\\\ A+2B=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=6,B=3.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6{e}^{2x}+3{e}^{4x}.\n$$",
